<http://dbpedia.org/resource/John_Lennon>	<http://dbpedia.org/property/description>	"Sample of \"Imagine\", Lennon's most widely known post-Beatles song. Like \"Give Peace a Chance\", the song became an anti-war anthem, but its lyrics offended religious groups. Lennon's explanation was: \"If you can imagine a world at peace, with no denominations of religion \u2013 not without religion, but without this 'my god is bigger than your god' thing \u2013 then it can be true.\""@en .
